# The build context is the repository root. The Dockerfile COPYs only the
# manifests, bun.lock and apps/api/, but `COPY apps/api/` takes everything under
# it, so these patterns match at ANY depth: a local apps/api/.env must never
# reach a layer, and a local node_modules or dist must not replace the ones the
# build installs and bundles. No .env.example is needed by the build.
**/node_modules
**/dist
**/.env
**/.env.*
**/*.log
signal-data
.git
.github
.worktrees
.vscode
.claude
docs
